# Reductions for the no-strong-FF step of 13.8.16(1)

The exchanged actor retains the actual component orbit, Sylow supplement,
moving element and marked projective product. Its orbit is self-centralizing,
so every noncentral section is faithful on the whole actor. The literal image
equivalence preserves every subgroup and the strong-offender condition.

The universal B.4.2 input retains the full source hypothesis and action list.
After a genuine irreducible reduction, its exact ratios leave only five
possible component models. Characteristic-two PSL₂ has no element of order
four, uniformly in the field exponent. Constructing the irreducible reduction
and excluding the five remaining models for characteristic-two PSL₂ remain separate obligations. This module
does not yet assert the intrinsic no-strong theorem or discharge the source
section dichotomy's two exclusions unconditionally.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), B.4.2,
printed pp.86–87, and 13.8.16(1), p.952 (PDF p.969).
-/
